    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an owner has an email, otherwise `'PHONE'`, exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThis is a standard Spring PetClinic app where the REST DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct mappers with derived fields. I followed that existing idiom (matching the `locality` / `displayName` derived-string fields):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression computing the value:\n   ```java\n   owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\"\n   ```\n\nResults:\n- `AcceptanceTest.corePhoneWhenNoEmail` \u2192 `PHONE` \u2713\n- `AcceptanceTest.functionalityEmailWhenPresent` \u2192 `EMAIL` \u2713\n- Full suite: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**",
